<title>DENMARK: Danish Jan/Feb retail sales rise.</title>
<headline>Danish Jan/Feb retail sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted retail sales index rose to 111.3 in January and 111.9 in February 1997 from 109.7 in December 1996,  the national statistics office said on Friday.</p>
<p>				   Feb 1997  Jan 1997   Dec 1996</p>
<p>  Seasonally adjusted volume 111.9     111.2	109.3</p>
<p>  Food, beverages,tobacco    106.4     106.9	103.4</p>
<p>  Clothing etc.		  110.9     107.8	109.3</p>
<p>  Other consumer goods	 119.9     118.7	117.7</p>
<p>NOTE - 1990 base = 100. The non-seasonally adjusted index for Jan-February 1997 was on average around 1.8 percent up on the same period in 1996, the statistics office said. Five analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a seasonally adjusted volume rise of 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
